---
import ModuleWrapper, { type _ModuleWrapper, type _ModuleHeader } from "@/components/ui/modules/ModuleWrapper.astro";

export interface Props extends _ModuleWrapper {}

const props = Astro.props;

const header: _ModuleHeader = {
	...props.header,
	title: props.header?.title || "Strengths and failure modes",
};
---

<ModuleWrapper {...{ ...props, header }}>
	<ul class="mb-6 ml-6 list-outside list-disc space-y-2">
		<li>I would rather succeed with a team than on my own. I have done it on my own often enough to know which I prefer.</li>
		<li>I say the thing rather than dance around it. Some people read that as blunt. It also means nobody has to guess where a project actually stands.</li>
		<li>I hold a high bar, for myself and for the people I work with. That is useful to someone who wants to get better at their job, and uncomfortable for someone who doesn't.</li>
		<li>I work at pace, and pace pushes people. Coaching is what I use to notice it, and I would rather be told I have the tempo wrong than find out later.</li>
		<li>
			I lose interest in work that repeats, so when a task keeps coming back I build the thing that does it instead. Most of what I have made that outlived me started as me refusing to do
			something twice.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<div id="culture" class="mb-6 rounded border border-line bg-sunk p-5">
		<p class="m-0 font-semibold">I fit best where the bar is high and people are direct about it.</p>
	</div>

	<div id="biggest-strengths" class="mb-6 scroll-mt-[150px] rounded border border-line bg-sunk p-5">
		<h3 class="mb-3 text-lg">My biggest strengths</h3>

		<ul class="ml-6 list-outside list-disc space-y-2">
			<li>Developing people is not something I picked up on the way to management. It was my first profession, five years of it, before I wrote software for a living.</li>
			<li>I am transparent about what I can do. If I don't know how, I'll go and find out.</li>
			<li>My <a href="#learning">curiosity</a> keeps me moving. How things work, how they should work, and how to improve them.</li>
			<li>Once I am set on a purpose I find a way. It doesn't always go to plan, but the important goal gets met.</li>
		</ul>
	</div>

	<div id="biggest-weaknesses" class="mb-6 scroll-mt-[150px] rounded border border-line bg-sunk p-5">
		<h3 class="mb-3 text-lg">My biggest weaknesses</h3>
		<ul class="ml-6 list-outside list-disc space-y-2">
			<li>I get bored easily, that's the other side of that <a href="#learning">curiosity</a>. I either push harder than I should or pull back and recharge on something else.</li>
			<li>I set ambitious goals and take on more than I should. However, planning, a purpose-driven team, and being clear about the shape is the difference between that landing and not.</li>
			<li>When I am deep in the work I lose track of how I am doing, so what it is costing me usually gets pointed out to me before I notice it.</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</ModuleWrapper>
